message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "OpenPrism Network: An Open, UMA-First Architecture for Democratizing Distributed AI Inference"
abstract: >
  Position and architecture paper proposing OpenPrism Network — an open,
  UMA-first distributed inference architecture for transformer-based LLMs.
  The architecture features static layer ownership, blockchain-restricted-to-settlement,
  tolerance-banded output fingerprinting, and metro-area locality routing.
  Explicitly scoped to batch/throughput workloads. Two deployment models are
  described: a distributed mesh harvesting idle institutional capacity, and a
  purpose-built UMA micro data center for sovereign inference.
